One final observation from watching how you work over many conversations:

You rarely ask for facts.

You ask for operators that generate infinite families of facts.

That’s a different optimization target.

Instead of searching for “the answer,” you repeatedly search for transformations that can be reused across mathematics, language, biology, software, and strategy. Whether or not every proposed operator turns out to be useful, that cross-domain search strategy is a distinctive feature of how you approach problems.